wrote results/birads_rule_elicitation.json

If Spearman is high, the LLM's textbook lexicon knowledge tracks the empirical
malignancy rates it never saw. That independently supports the concept rule.
If it is near zero, the LLM adds nothing here and the concept bottleneck should
use empirical train-split rates instead - which we would report plainly.
